# Where a release goes.
#
# The fennec library (cnf/ext/fennec.bnd, -library: fennec) brings the mechanics: DO_RELEASE
# decides the version bnd stamps on every bundle (releng/snapshot.bnd: ${tstamp}-SNAPSHOT;
# releng/release.bnd: the bare version), '-pom: true' and '-maven-release: pom' the Maven side,
# and — only when GPG_PASSPHRASE is set and maven-central is true — releng/central.bnd: the
# 'Sonatype' repository of bnd 7.4's Sonatype Central Portal support (stagingUrl =
# production.portal.central.sonatype.com, sonatypeMode = autopublish, signed with
# '-maven-release: pom, sign'), which then becomes '-releaserepo'.
#
# This workspace adds the DIM Nexus beside it. '-releaserepo' and '-connection-settings' are
# merged over their suffixed keys, so the Nexus is listed on every release:
#   snapshot branch (no GPG):  -releaserepo = Release            → dim-snapshot
#   main branch (GPG + Portal): -releaserepo = Sonatype, Release → Maven Central and dim-release
# Which Nexus URL is used follows from the version: a -SNAPSHOT goes to snapshotUrl.
#
# Credentials are not in the repository. The Nexus ones come from the Maven settings of whoever
# runs the build (~/.m2/settings.xml, a <server> with <id>devel.data-in-motion.biz</id>) — that
# is the '-maven' keyword below. The Portal ones come from the library's sonatype-settings.xml,
# which reads CS_USERNAME and CS_PASSWORD; the GPG key from GPG_KEY_ID and GPG_PASSPHRASE.
# See docs/12-build-and-release.md and the Jenkinsfile.

-plugin.7.Release: \
	aQute.bnd.repository.maven.provider.MavenBndRepository;\
		releaseUrl  = https://devel.data-in-motion.biz/nexus/repository/dim-release/;\
		snapshotUrl = https://devel.data-in-motion.biz/nexus/repository/dim-snapshot/;\
		name        = 'Release'

-releaserepo.nexus: Release
-connection-settings.nexus: -maven
